    {
     "flag": "river_town_logs_back",
     "lines": [
      "Six logs home. Dried, stacked, counted twice. Thank you, Geometra.",
      "Poplar's honest wood. Light, straight, quick to grow. A lot like me, my husband used to say. He meant the quick part."
     ]
    },
    {
     "lines": [
      "Mind the saw. Mind the logs. Mind your feet.",
      "The flood took six of my best logs downriver. Six. I counted the empty spaces."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "sleepy": [
    "Zzz… measure twice… cut once… measure again…"
   ],
   "topics": [
    {
     "id": "sawmill",
     "label": "How long has the sawmill been here?",
     "lines": [
      "My husband built it in seventy-one. I ran the books, then I ran the saw, then I ran everything.",
      "We plant a poplar for every one we cut. Ten years and they're as tall as the church."
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "logs",
     "label": "Where did your logs go?",
     "lines": [
      "Downriver, mostly. Some only as far as the willows. One's under Wanda's dance hall, I'd bet my glasses on it."
     ]
    }
   ],
